{"id": "85915", "name": "חוקי לוגריתמים – ln(x^m·y) בעזרת p = ln x, q = ln y (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>Given that \\(p={{CT:0}}\\) and \\(q={{CT:1}}\\).</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Then give \\({{CT:2}}\\) as a function of \\(p\\) and \\(q\\).</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans1]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">The laws of logarithms</b><br>Given \\(p={{CT:0}}\\) and \\(q={{CT:1}}\\) then, using first the logarithm of a product (the sum of the logarithms) and then the logarithm of a power (the exponent comes out as a factor),<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:2}} = \\ln \\left({{CT:3}}\\right)+{{CT:1}} = {{CT:4}} = {{CT:5}}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "EqualComAss", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "mp_plus_q", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "LGE-LLG-TRUE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "LGE-LLG-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "p^m+q", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "POWER", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">You seem to have that \\(\\ln\\left(x^{{CT:6}}\\right)=\\left(\\ln \\left( x \\right) \\right)^{{CT:6}}\\). This is not a law of logarithms: for example, for \\(x=e\\) the left side is \\({{CT:6}}\\) and the right side is \\(1\\). A power inside a logarithm comes out as a factor: \\[\\ln \\left({{CT:3}}\\right) = {{CT:7}}.\\]</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "LGE-LLG-1-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "m*p*q", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "NO_ADDITION", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">You seem to have that \\({{CT:2}}\\) is \\(\\ln \\left({{CT:3}}\\right)\\) multiplied by \\({{CT:1}}\\). The logarithm of a product is the sum of the logarithms: \\[{{CT:2}}=\\ln \\left({{CT:3}}\\right)+{{CT:1}}.\\]</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "LGE-LLG-2-FALSE", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["log_x", "log_xm", "log_xmy", "log_y", "m", "mlog_x", "mlog_x_plus_log_y", "mp_plus_q", "xm", "xmy"], "nvariants": 4}